//? Title: Union merge: actual duplicate-discard decisions
//? Subtitle: Actual native state and retained original experiments
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Merging sorted lists while retaining each value once should preserve ordering
and discard duplicate identities. A heap of current list fronts provides both
the merged order and explicit emission decisions.
)

\toc

> The method

The heap minimum is no larger than any unexposed element because each run is
sorted. Emit a popped value only if it differs from the last output. Induction
yields sorted set union. Every input identity is still pushed and popped once:
deduplication shrinks output, not input traversal. For N keys over R nonempty
runs, work is O(N log(R+1)) plus validation, with O(R) heap storage.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/union_merge_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::k_way_merge_trace({{1, 1}, {1, 2}}, true);
    std::print("| popped value | list | input index | emitted |\n|---:|---:|---:|---|\n");
    for (auto q : r.steps)
        if (q.kind == a::MergeHeapKind::Pop)
            std::print("|{}|{}|{}|{}|\n", q.value, q.list, q.index, q.emitted);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Runs[1,1] and[1,2]");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual pops", r.work.pops));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0}, std::format("Actual union {}", r.values));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/union_merge_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| popped value | list | input index | emitted |
|---:|---:|---:|---|
|1|0|0|true|
|1|0|1|false|
|1|1|0|false|
|2|1|1|true|
\image(figures/union_merge_tiny.svg)
// result_end
